<title>GERMANY: IWH institute sees German 1997 GDP at 2.0 pct.</title>
<headline>IWH institute sees German 1997 GDP at 2.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HALLE, Germany 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Halle economic research institute (IWH) on Friday gave the following economic forecasts for Germany. (In percent unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    GDP				1997	 1998</p>
<p>    Pan German		     +2.0	 +2.5</p>
<p>    West German		    +2.0	 +2.5</p>
<p>    East German		    +2.4	 +2.8</p>
<p>PRIVATE CONSUMPTION</p>
<p>    Pan German		     +0.3	 +1.6</p>
<p>PUBLIC CONSUMPTION</p>
<p>    Pan German		     +1.7 pct   +0.9</p>
<p>UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    Pan German			4.330 million 4.325 million</p>
<p>    West German		     3.030 million 2.995 million</p>
<p>    East German		     1.300 million 1.330 million</p>
<p>UNEMPLOYMENT RATE</p>
<p>    Pan German			+11.3     +11.3</p>
<p>    West German		     +9.8	+ 9.7</p>
<p>    East German		     +17.5     + 18.0</p>
<p>INVESTMENT IN FIXED ASSETS</p>
<p>    Pan German			 +0.4     +2.7</p>
<p>    (Of which equipment)	   +3.4     +6.0</p>
<p>    (Of which buildings)	   -1.5     +0.5</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p>    Pan German			 +7.0     +6.8</p>
<p>    IMPORTS			    +4.5     +4.7</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
